  "notes": "バテる may come from \"batter\" (as in exhausting oneself through repeated effort) or from ⟦{果|は}てる→果てる：28565_hateru⟧ (to reach the end/be exhausted). It's particularly associated with summer heat exhaustion (⟦{夏|なつ}バテ→夏バテ：15545_natsubate⟧).\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is a casual/colloquial verb. In formal contexts, use ⟦{疲労|ひろう}→疲労：13603_hirou⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ or ⟦{疲|つか}れ→疲れる：00901_tsukareru⟧⟦{切|き}る→切る：02693_kiru⟧.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{夏|なつ}バテ→夏バテ：15545_natsubate⟧: summer fatigue/heat exhaustion\n- バテ⟦{気味|ぎみ}→気味：27635_gimi⟧: feeling somewhat exhausted\n- バテて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧: to be in an exhausted state\n\nASPECT (ている):\nバテて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates an ongoing state of exhaustion.",
